{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102083","id":2299553371,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6JEGZb","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102083","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102083.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102083.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102083","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102083/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102083/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102083/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/26e0c9a4c9591397de11173ba12155ad10046f27","number":102083,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Implement `@if_features` annotation for feature-based code stripping","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"After checking some of the proposals on adding some preprocessing abilities to GDScript, and aware of certain real-world needs on this, I started trying to implement something that would be as unintrusive as possible. The result is this PR.\r\n\r\nWhat I'm adding here is a `@if_features` annotation that works this way:\r\n- It can only be applied to function members of classes, either the main class in a source file or an inner class.\r\n- It accepts zero or more string arguments. They are meant to correspond to features declared by platforms and export presets.\r\n- Users have to apply the annotation to each function in a group of equally-named functions, knowing that only the one matching will be taken into account at runtime.\r\n- If multiple features are stated, they are treated with an implicit _and_.\r\n- The annotation having zero arguments means the function annotated is the default one, the one to be picked in case none of the others with the same name fits.\r\n- From a set of equally-named functions using the annotation, only the first one fitting is taken into account, unless it's a default one, which can be overtaken by the first one with one or more features that comes later.\r\n- At script edit time, the annotation is only honored to make it possible to have multiple equally-named functions.\r\n- At runtime from an editor build, the annotation is resolved at runtime, against the features advertised at the moment.\r\n- At export time, the script is preprocessed to effectively strip out the functions whose target features don't fit what the target platform and export preset declare. (Stripping is performed by replacing the lines corresponding to the unmatching functions' annotations, declaration and body, with blank lines.)\r\n\r\nExample (more in the test case included in the commit):\r\n```GDScript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\t_implementation()\r\n\r\n@if_features() # No features means this is the default. Used in case no other fits.\r\nfunc _implementation():\r\n\tprint(\"Other OS...\")\r\n\r\n@if_features(\"windows\")\r\nfunc _implementation():\r\n\tprint(\"Windows!\")\r\n\r\n@if_features(\"linuxbsd\", \"s3tc\")\r\nfunc _implementation():\r\n\tprint(\"Linuxxx with S3TC texture compression!\")\r\n\r\n@if_features(\"linuxbsd\", \"astc\")\r\nfunc _implementation():\r\n\tprint(\"Linuxxx with ASTC texture compression!\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n**UPDATE:**\r\nA `runtime` feature is added, which is advertised when the script is run in the game, regardless it's an editor build or not, but not if run on the editor. See [this comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102083#issuecomment-2627812329).\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```GDScript\r\n@tool\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n\tdo_some_setup_needed_for_editor_and_runtime()\r\n\r\n@if_features(\"runtime\")\r\nfunc _process(time):\r\n\trun_the_gameplay_part()\r\n```\r\n---\r\n\r\nAdditional work for the future:\r\n- Support the annotation on other items, not only functions.\r\n- Add tests of the export-time stripping.\r\n- Support the annotation in other languages (i.e., C#). **UPDATE:** Other languages may not really need this.\r\n~- Support tool scripts. **UPDATE:** A tool script can just perform regular runtime feature checks.~\r\n\r\nImplements, kind of, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4234.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"",